"""Editorial question designs for cinema, documentary making, and acting."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


CINEMA = """history_origins|A Film Form Takes Shape|Which early production or exhibition practice shaped a named film form?|Compare dated films, trade records, and local exhibition context.
famous_examples|A Landmark Film Revisited|What formal choice made a named film influential, and who called it so?|Analyze the film and dated reception rather than repeat a canon label.
hidden_stories|Labor Behind a Film|Whose credited and uncredited work shaped a named scene?|Check credits, production records, interviews, and competing accounts.
beginner_explainers|How a Scene Communicates|How do framing, sound, performance, and cutting guide one interpretation?|Show the sequence and distinguish observation from interpretation.
advanced_concepts|Form and Spectatorship|How does a film's viewpoint position its audience across a sequence?|Compare formal evidence with specific theories and reception studies.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Lost or Disputed Film|Which version, credit, or release history remains uncertain?|Separate surviving material, catalog records, and speculation.
technology_innovation|A Film Tool in Practice|How did a camera, sound, or projection change alter a particular production?|Trace equipment and decisions without claiming technology alone caused an aesthetic shift.
people_personalities|A Filmmaker's Choices|Which documented decisions shaped a named film?|Compare work, drafts, collaborators, and attributed interviews.
major_events|A Screening that Changed Circulation|How did a festival, censorship decision, or distribution deal affect one film?|Use dated programs, rulings, contracts, and audience records.
how_it_works|From Shot to Sequence|How do shot order and duration change what viewers can infer?|Compare cuts of the same bounded passage when available.
rise_fall|A Film's Changing Reputation|How did critical or public response shift after release?|Sample dated reviews and access conditions across periods.
then_vs_now|One Film Across Formats|What changes between an original release and a later restoration or stream?|Identify source element, aspect ratio, sound, and exhibition conditions.
future_developments|A Changing Exhibition Practice|What evidence supports a proposed shift in film access or presentation?|Specify place, period, audience, and uncertainty.
myths_vs_facts|A Familiar Cinema Origin Story|Which part of a common first-film claim survives archival checking?|Define the claimed first and compare dated records.
documentary_stories|A Film's Production Trail|How did a script, shoot, edit, and release shape one surviving film?|Follow versioned artifacts and testimony with provenance.
creative_brief|A Film's Stated Aim|What was the production trying to communicate at a documented stage?|Compare brief or script with finished work without assuming one authorial intent.
materials_and_tools|Film Stock or Digital Capture|How did a chosen medium constrain one visual decision?|Identify actual stock, sensor, lens, and workflow records.
process_breakdown|Making a Scene|Which decisions moved a scene from script to final cut?|Trace drafts, shot plans, takes, and editorial record.
composition_choice|Meaning in a Frame|How do placement, movement, and offscreen space shape one scene?|Use timecoded frame comparisons and alternative readings.
collaborative_authorship|Who Made the Film?|Which contributions by writer, performers, crew, and editor are documented?|Check credits and records; avoid assigning one person every choice.
adaptation_across_media|A Story Becomes Film|What changes when a named source becomes a screen sequence?|Compare source passage, screenplay, and finished scene.
audience_reception|Who Saw This Film?|How did different audiences encounter and interpret a film?|Use situated reviews, surveys, or oral histories with sampling limits.
cultural_context|A Film in Its Place|Which local production and viewing conditions shaped its meanings?|Identify language, policy, funding, and reception without treating a culture as uniform.
preservation_restoration|Which Film Version Survives?|What does a restoration reconstruct from incomplete elements?|Document source materials, interventions, and unresolved gaps.
rights_and_attribution|Ownership and Film Credit|Who can document authorship and reuse permissions for a clip?|Separate creative credit, copyright, license, and archival custody.
style_comparison|Two Film Styles|Which visible and audible choices distinguish two bounded sequences?|Compare matched functions, dates, and exhibition formats.
creative_failure|A Scene That Did Not Work|What evidence shows why a production revised or abandoned a scene?|Use drafts and production testimony; avoid inferring failure from taste.
field_textual_form|Reading a Film Sequence|How do image, dialogue, and sound organize narrative information?|Timecode formal choices before interpreting them.
field_performance_choice|A Performance on Screen|How does acting interact with framing and editing in one scene?|Compare available takes or cuts and credit collaborators.
field_audience_history|A Film's Viewers Over Time|How did access and audience response change across releases?|Distinguish documented viewers from hypothetical audience.
field_translation_or_adaptation|Subtitles and Meaning|What choices change when dialogue is subtitled or dubbed?|Compare language versions with translators and release contexts.
field_critical_reception|A Review Becomes a Reputation|How did a specific critical judgment spread or face challenge?|Trace dated reviews, citations, and later reassessments.
"""

DOCUMENTARY = """history_origins|A Documentary Practice Emerges|Which specific production practice changed nonfiction filmmaking?|Compare dated films, production notes, and contemporary debate.
famous_examples|A Documentary Claim Examined|How does a named film support its central factual claim?|Trace footage, documents, interviews, and omitted counterevidence.
hidden_stories|Subjects Behind the Camera|How did participants influence or contest the finished account?|Use consent records, production testimony, and participant responses.
beginner_explainers|What Makes Footage Evidence?|What can one recorded scene establish and what lies outside its frame?|Identify date, location, recorder, edit, and corroboration.
advanced_concepts|Truth in the Edit|How do selection, ordering, and narration change a factual inference?|Compare raw or earlier material with the release when available.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Documentary's Unverified Claim|Which evidence is missing for a key assertion?|Name the claim, search primary records, and mark uncertainty.
technology_innovation|A New Recording Method|How did a tool alter access, intimacy, or verification in a production?|Document equipment and subject conditions, not just image quality.
people_personalities|A Director and Their Subjects|Whose choices shaped a sensitive scene?|Check filmmaker and participant accounts against footage and records.
major_events|A Documentary Changes Public Debate|What documented response followed one film's release?|Separate temporal sequence from causal impact.
how_it_works|Building a Verified Sequence|How are actuality footage, archive, narration, and graphics sourced?|Make a shot-level evidence and rights map.
rise_fall|A Claim Under Challenge|How did new evidence change a documentary's account?|Compare original claim, correction, and subsequent response.
then_vs_now|Revisiting a Filmed Subject|What changed after the original filming, and who can verify it?|Date all follow-up evidence and seek subject response.
future_developments|Documentary Distribution Choices|Which current access route changes who can see or challenge a film?|Specify market, platform terms, and reachable audience.
myths_vs_facts|The Camera Never Lies?|Which filmed details are real yet misleading without context?|Show framing, timing, selection, and corroboration.
documentary_stories|An Investigation on Film|How did a production move from question to defensible public claim?|Trace leads, verification, dissent, and revisions.
creative_brief|The Documentary's Promise|What question and duty to participants did the initial brief establish?|Compare proposal, consent language, and finished film.
materials_and_tools|Camera, Recorder, and Archive|Which capture and archive choices affect evidence quality?|Track metadata, continuity, access, and source provenance.
process_breakdown|From Research to Release|What checks occur between interview, transcription, edit, and publication?|Map each step to its accountable record.
composition_choice|Framing a Real Person|What interpretation does a portrait shot invite?|Compare framing with participant context and explicit factual claims.
collaborative_authorship|Whose Documentary Is It?|What did participants, researchers, editors, and translators contribute?|Check agreements, credits, and conflicting testimony.
adaptation_across_media|Records Become Scenes|How did a written record become a reenactment or visual account?|Label reconstruction and compare it with the source.
audience_reception|A Documentary Meets Its Subjects|How did filmed people and viewers respond to publication?|Separate documented responses from predicted impact.
cultural_context|Filming Across Communities|How do language and local power affect access and interpretation?|Use local expertise and participant review where appropriate.
preservation_restoration|Preserving Documentary Evidence|What source material survives behind the final cut?|Inventory originals, transcripts, metadata, and restrictions.
rights_and_attribution|Consent and Clip Rights|Which permissions and duties govern footage reuse?|Separate legal release, continuing ethics, and archive terms.
style_comparison|Observational and Narrated Accounts|How do two approaches support different kinds of claims?|Compare similar subjects and disclose intervention.
creative_failure|A Documentary Correction|What verification gap required a cut or public correction?|Trace error, affected person, remedy, and recorded update.
field_shot_design|Shooting an Actual Event|What did camera position capture or exclude?|Record access constraints and missing viewpoints.
field_production_workflow|Consent Through Production|When and how could a participant understand or revisit consent?|Check scripts, releases, translation, and changed risks.
field_sound_choices|A Documentary Soundtrack|Which sounds are location records, wild tracks, or added effects?|Audit source and labeling against the impression created.
field_editing_rhythm|Cutting an Interview|Does compression preserve a speaker's meaning and chronology?|Compare transcript, source recording, and final sequence.
field_distribution_format|Publishing the Film|What changes when a film is screened, broadcast, or clipped online?|Check context, permissions, corrections, and audience reach.
"""

ACTING = """history_origins|A Performance Tradition Traced|Which documented training or staging practice shaped a particular role?|Use dated scripts, rehearsal records, and practitioner accounts.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Performance Revisited|What observable choices make a named performance distinctive?|Analyze recorded work and situated criticism without mind-reading.
hidden_stories|The Ensemble's Contribution|Who helped create a remembered scene beyond its star?|Check credits, rehearsals, blocking, and collaborator testimony.
beginner_explainers|Choices in a Scene|How do objective, timing, listening, and movement affect a short exchange?|Show a bounded scene and compare alternatives.
advanced_concepts|Acting Across Takes|How can a performance remain coherent when scenes are shot out of order?|Trace continuity notes and available takes.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disputed Performance Credit|What evidence can establish who performed or devised a moment?|Separate contracts, credits, footage, and later recollection.
technology_innovation|Performance Capture and Acting|Which actor choices are preserved or altered in a captured performance?|Compare recorded action, animation, and credited collaborators.
people_personalities|A Role Built with a Director|Which decisions can be attributed to actor, director, or editor?|Use rehearsal and production records rather than inferred intent.
major_events|A Staging Change|How did a documented production decision change a role's delivery?|Compare dated versions and contemporary accounts.
how_it_works|Listening on Camera|How does a reaction shot shape the scene's meaning?|Compare performance, framing, and cut order.
rise_fall|A Performance Reassessed|Why did critical response to a role change over time?|Trace dated reviews and changed viewing context.
then_vs_now|One Role, Different Productions|Which choices change when performers restage the same text?|Compare performance records within their media limits.
future_developments|Changing Actor Workflows|Which emerging production practice changes preparation or credit?|Specify contract, production type, and documented effects.
myths_vs_facts|A Single Acting Method?|Does a performer use one fixed technique for every role?|Check training and production accounts against work.
documentary_stories|Building a Role|How did documented rehearsal and production choices shape a performance?|Follow drafts, coaching, takes, and final edit.
creative_brief|What Was the Actor Asked to Do?|How did script and direction frame a role at a given stage?|Compare brief, rehearsal notes, and finished work.
materials_and_tools|The Actor's Working Tools|How do costume, prop, set, and microphone affect delivery?|Identify actual equipment and performance constraints.
process_breakdown|From Audition to Final Cut|What changes between casting, rehearsal, shooting, and edit?|Track versioned evidence and who made each choice.
composition_choice|Body in the Frame|How does position and movement change a character relationship?|Analyze blocking, camera placement, and alternatives.
collaborative_authorship|Making a Performance Together|How do partner, director, editor, and crew shape a role?|Credit documented contributions without erasing actor agency.
adaptation_across_media|A Role on Stage and Screen|What changes in voice, timing, and gesture across formats?|Compare specific productions and recording limits.
audience_reception|How Viewers Read a Role|Which reactions are actually documented for a performance?|Use situated reviews or audience research with sampling limits.
cultural_context|Performance in Translation|How does language or casting context change interpretation?|Compare versions with local expertise and avoid universal claims.
preservation_restoration|A Performance in the Archive|What can a recording preserve or miss about live acting?|Identify capture angle, sound, edit, and audience context.
rights_and_attribution|Consent and Performance Use|Which agreement governs reuse, dubbing, or digital alteration of a performance?|Check actual contract and jurisdiction before asserting rights.
style_comparison|Two Approaches to a Role|Which observable choices distinguish two performers in the same scene?|Compare matched text and production contexts.
creative_failure|A Rehearsal Revision|Why was a performance choice changed before release?|Use documented notes and actor response; avoid judging from rumor.
field_shot_design|Acting for a Close-Up|Which smaller gestures become legible at a chosen frame size?|Compare takes and lens or camera context.
field_production_workflow|A Safe Rehearsal Process|How were boundaries, direction, and changes communicated to performers?|Use documented protocols and participant accounts.
field_sound_choices|Voice as Performance|How do breath, pace, dubbing, and recording alter a role?|Compare source and final tracks and credit voice work.
field_editing_rhythm|Performance Made in the Cut|How do take choice and reaction timing alter an actor's apparent intention?|Compare available material and avoid attributing editor choices to actor.
field_distribution_format|The Same Role on Different Screens|How does cinema, television, or phone playback change perceivable detail?|Specify mix, framing, display, and viewer conditions.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("368", "368_cinema", CINEMA,
                  "Cinema as collaboratively made and circulated moving-image art, examined through film form, production, exhibition, preservation, and situated reception.",
                  "timecoded films and versions, production records, credits, archive catalogs, dated criticism, exhibition records, and participant accounts",
                  "Identify film, version, place, and period. Separate what is visible or documented from interpretation, causal impact, and inferred creator intent.")
    revise_domain("369", "369_documentary_making", DOCUMENTARY,
                  "Documentary making as accountable nonfiction production with verifiable claims, traceable footage, participant consent, editing transparency, and corrections.",
                  "original footage and metadata, transcripts, releases, primary records, archive provenance, production logs, participant responses, and documented corrections",
                  "A filmed scene is partial evidence, not full context. Verify factual assertions independently, document reconstruction and editing, and assess consent and participant risk throughout distribution.")
    revise_domain("370", "370_acting", ACTING,
                  "Acting as a collaborative, situated performance practice shaped by rehearsal, partners, direction, camera, sound, edit, working conditions, and audience reception.",
                  "recorded performances, scripts, rehearsal and continuity notes, credits, contracts where available, actor and collaborator interviews, and dated criticism",
                  "Describe observable choices and documented decisions without diagnosing a performer or inferring private intent. Keep consent, credit, and working context specific to the production.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
